  "_about": "Food pairing tags for Pour Choices (round 33, 20 Nov 2026). Read by scrapers/pairing_tags.py after each scrape (stamps 'pairing_tags' onto every product in data/products.json) and by index.html as a fallback when a product has no tags yet. One rules file, so the app and the scraper can never disagree. Each tag: 'categories' = the scraped category the product must be in; 'match' = words in the name (case does not matter); 'exclude' = words that rule it out; 'default' = true means every product in those categories gets this tag unless it matched another tag in the same 'group'. Accents are removed from names and rules before matching (rosé -> rose), so the regular expressions behave the same in Python and JavaScript. Labels shown to shoppers and the menu presets live in index.html.",
